{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956964-reality-vs-game-mechanics","id":956964,"title":"Reality vs. Game Mechanics","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-24T07:45:32-07:00","id":956964,"title":"Reality vs. Game Mechanics","content":"Hi all,<br /> <br /> I'm new to Chronicles of Darkness, and also new to Storytelling. My troupe is also new to the system.<br /> <br /> We did our first session last Sunday, and it mostly went well. But there was one issue that kept cropping up - called head shots.<br /> <br /> In real life, generally a gun shot to the head pretty much = instant death. But in game terms, it only knocks a person down a point or two. If it was an actual monster, I think I could have made a better case for it surviving, but these were humans (possessed humans, but still human).<br /> <br /> How do you deal with this in your games? Do you give them an extra point or two of damage? Do you give them a clean kill? Or do you just stick with the rules as written and mark down another point of damage? My group was a little bit frustrated by this because they kept expecting to get a more dramatic result from their successful head shots. <br /> <br /> Would love to hear how more experienced Storytellers handle this sort of thing.<br /> <br /> Thanks!<br /> <br /> Valerie","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12106-digigirl","name":"Digigirl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T07:50:00-07:00","id":956966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Digigirl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956964-reality-vs-game-mechanics#post956964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi all,<br /> <br /> I'm new to Chronicles of Darkness, and also new to Storytelling. My troupe is also new to the system.<br /> <br /> We did our first session last Sunday, and it mostly went well. But there was one issue that kept cropping up - called head shots.<br /> <br /> In real life, generally a gun shot to the head pretty much = instant death. But in game terms, it only knocks a person down a point or two. If it was an actual monster, I think I could have made a better case for it surviving, but these were humans (possessed humans, but still human).<br /> <br /> How do you deal with this in your games? Do you give them an extra point or two of damage? Do you give them a clean kill? Or do you just stick with the rules as written and mark down another point of damage? My group was a little bit frustrated by this because they kept expecting to get a more dramatic result from their successful head shots.<br /> <br /> Would love to hear how more experienced Storytellers handle this sort of thing.<br /> <br /> Thanks!<br /> <br /> Valerie</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hi, Valerie! Welcome!<br /> <br /> There's a mechanic for called shots. To be honest, I'm not big on combat in my games, so I don't have the mechanic memorized, and I'm not home to check the book. But one does exist. I'm sure other posters will be able to elaborate. Sorry I couldn't be of more help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T08:10:25-07:00","id":956971,"title":"","content":"Hi Valerie,<br /> <br /> I think the problem is that in the common language, &quot;Head Shot&quot; means &quot;A shot between the eyes&quot;. Which it is not. It can be a shot in the jaw, a grazing hit to the temple, or any other kind of shot. But if you want that kind of combat, there's the Down and Dirty combat mechanic which can allow for such a combat scene, just be aware that your players can die pretty quickly in such a system.<br /> <br /> If your players expect to be able to take a penalty to their shot and kill people in one hit, they should expect to be killed in one hit. Rules work both ways (unless you decide otherwise, which is also fine, it's your game after all).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T08:13:15-07:00","id":956973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Digigirl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956964-reality-vs-game-mechanics#post956964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi all,<br /> <br /> I'm new to Chronicles of Darkness, and also new to Storytelling. My troupe is also new to the system.<br /> <br /> We did our first session last Sunday, and it mostly went well. But there was one issue that kept cropping up - called head shots.<br /> <br /> In real life, generally a gun shot to the head pretty much = instant death. But in game terms, it only knocks a person down a point or two. If it was an actual monster, I think I could have made a better case for it surviving, but these were humans (possessed humans, but still human).<br /> <br /> How do you deal with this in your games? Do you give them an extra point or two of damage? Do you give them a clean kill? Or do you just stick with the rules as written and mark down another point of damage? My group was a little bit frustrated by this because they kept expecting to get a more dramatic result from their successful head shots.<br /> <br /> Would love to hear how more experienced Storytellers handle this sort of thing.<br /> <br /> Thanks!<br /> <br /> Valerie</div> </div> </div> </div>So, in 2E at least, head shots have some neat advantages: if you do at least the target's Size in damage, they'll get the Stunned Tilt, which denies them their defense and action for the next turn. Which usually means you can follow up with another attack and presumably finish them off. Also, since you've done on average 5 damage, they're likely almost dead since with a gun you're talking lethal damage. You could also argue for some sort of Condition like Blind, Crippled, almost certainly Beaten Down (if you're playing with it).<br /> <br /> Here's the thing though: a hit doesn't have to mean you've snagged them solidly between the eyes. That might be the case if you're using Down and Dirty Combat, and your intent was to kill the target, but in regular combat the dice mean what they say. You figure out what it means when a PC gets shot in the head, but not enough damage to kill them happens: typically I'd assume that means they were hit indirectly somehow. Given how fragile our brains are, I could even see the bullet actually missing, but getting close enough that it still causes &quot;damage&quot;.<br /> <br /> If you want guns to be a little more lethal when it comes to called shots, you might just give them the Stun quality: if a weapon has the stun quality, you use half the target's Size to determine if you've stunned them instead of their whole size.<br /> <br /> At any rate, if I'm running NPCs and they get shot in the head, the fight is most certainly going to end unless the PCs have made it clear that they will kill the NPC, in which case they are going to try to <i>run away as fast as possible</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T09:24:35-07:00","id":957010,"title":"","content":"Actually, Headshots allow you to stun at Size-1 or something like that. You always stun when you hit for Size damage. And Stunned target may still take their action if they are willing to burn a Willpower point on that. In general, aiming for a head isn't a very good tactic, both in real life and in the game.<br /> And yeah, remember that you get to narrate the effect of the shot. If you don't feel that numbers feel right for a direct shot to the head, make it a grazing hit, or even say that target didn't hit at all, but is scared and exhausted from avoiding gunfire. In the end, health track exists to check how much target can take before going down, not to simulate effects of wounds.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> To elaborate, &quot;instant kill&quot; zone for head shots is actually pretty small. Hitting the dead center is best represented by a shot that scores, well, a lot of successes = lots of damage. It's much more efficient to aim for the center of the body than to try to score a perfect head shot; non-perfect body mass shot will probably hit something anyway and deal damage, while non-perfect head shot will probably not hit at all or don't do much damage. Headshots are overrated. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 08-24-2016, 12:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T09:26:46-07:00","id":957012,"title":"","content":"A house-rule you can implement to put emphasis on how dangerous is to target someone's head would be to upgrade the damage type used when targeting it. Guns &amp; Crowbars do Aggravated, bare fists do Lethal. Boxers can kill you with a well placed uppercut - or cause enough trauma to compromise the nervous system heavily - but that's better modeled with Persistent Conditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T09:33:21-07:00","id":957014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956964-reality-vs-game-mechanics?p=957010#post957010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, Headshots allow you to stun at Size-1 or something like that. You always stun when you hit for Size damage. And Stunned target may still take their action if they are willing to burn a Willpower point on that. In general, aiming for a head isn't a very good tactic, both in real life and in the game.<br /> And yeah, remember that you get to narrate the effect of the shot. If you don't feel that numbers feel right for a direct shot to the head, make it a grazing hit, or even say that target didn't hit at all, but is scared and exhausted from avoiding gunfire. In the end, health track exists to check how much target can take before going down, not to simulate effects of wounds.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> To elaborate, &quot;instant kill&quot; zone for head shots is actually pretty small. Hitting the dead center is best represented by a shot that scores, well, a lot of successes = lots of damage. It's much more efficient to aim for the center of the body than to try to score a perfect head shot; non-perfect body mass shot will probably hit something anyway and deal damage, while non-perfect head shot will probably not hit at all or don't do much damage. Headshots are overrated. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, I double-checked while I was waiting for my lunch to heat up (bringing RPG books to the office makes things so much less boring <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ), it's Size-1 if you target the head. So typically you only need to do 4 damage, which is pretty easy with a gun since they don't get their Defense and the smallest gun has a 1 damage rating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T09:44:52-07:00","id":957021,"title":"","content":"Eh, to do that reliably you need dicepool of something like 9 or 12 dice after the headshot penalty (what was it? I'm away from books). If I remember correctly, penalty on aiming to the head would probably net you that extra damage anyway.<br /> Of course, often forgotten advantage of headshots in the game is that people love donning super heavy armors only to leave their faces vulnerable :P. <br /> Anyway, if you want to make headshots more attractive, you might consider changing the benefit to something like, I don't know, let's call it LETHAL QUALITY<br /> <br /> LETHAL QUALITY: Reroll all successes on the roll and add any resulting successes to damage dealt.<br /> <br /> So a graze will still be a graze, but a 3 damage hit might turn into 4 damage hit. <br /> <br /> Remember, however, that this game isn't balanced about instant kills; in fact, ChroD doesn't like one-turn kills too much. It's easy to put someone at serious disadvantage, but it's hard to finish them off in one turn (unless multiple attackers are trying to off on person); someone who want's to run away almost always can do so in this game.<br /> Which is ok, because GMs don't have to pull punches and players can engage the monster for a turn before realizing HOLY NINJAS LET'S RUN AWAY.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T11:26:48-07:00","id":957066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956964-reality-vs-game-mechanics?p=957021#post957021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">LETHAL QUALITY: Reroll all successes on the roll and add any resulting successes to damage dealt.</div> </div> </div> </div>So...... 8-again?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T11:36:09-07:00","id":957073,"title":"","content":"Haha, kinda! That's what I get for writing when grilling :P. It's hard to make headshots balanced, and it seems that game devs decided to err on the side of underpowered than overpowered (a good choice).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T11:52:47-07:00","id":957082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956964-reality-vs-game-mechanics?p=957021#post957021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, to do that reliably you need dicepool of something like 9 or 12 dice after the headshot penalty (what was it? I'm away from books). If I remember correctly, penalty on aiming to the head would probably net you that extra damage anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. The penalty for targeting the head is -3, so unless they're wearing armor it's a wash in terms of causing stun and a -1 on actual damage caused, on average. That said, getting around most armor shouldn't be underestimated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956964-reality-vs-game-mechanics?p=957012#post957012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A house-rule you can implement to put emphasis on how dangerous is to target someone's head would be to upgrade the damage type used when targeting it. Guns &amp; Crowbars do Aggravated, bare fists do Lethal. Boxers can kill you with a well placed uppercut.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually really like this suggestion. I would probably further increase the dice penalty for targeting the head in this case, though. Maybe -5? That would make the head harder to hit than the hand. I don't know how well that simulates reality, but feels like about the right penalty for upgrading the damage type to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T12:03:30-07:00","id":957089,"title":"","content":"In reality, you get a T-shaped zone of &quot;get hit here and you are in really bad shape&quot; around your nose and eyes (but not forehead) which is pretty small, but is #1 lethal thing to aim for. However, rest of the head is a worse target in both &quot;how easy it is to hit&quot; and &quot;how lethal it is&quot; than center of the chest (which is also easiest target to hit), which is #1 target and #2 most lethal area to be hit. <br /> The &quot;stun&quot; thing is actually pretty realistic, because being shot in the head will &quot;stun&quot; you for sure, even if it might not be enough stopping power to get you down. <br /> <br /> In general, game follows reality &quot;aim for the center of the mass, because it's easy and lethal&quot; by making non-aimed shots the most dangerous shots - you get your full dicepool, which translates in more succeses, and with Hurt Locker, you can also get BLEEDING tilt this way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T12:38:06-07:00","id":957112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956964-reality-vs-game-mechanics?p=957089#post957089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In reality, you get a T-shaped zone of &amp;quot;get hit here and you are in really bad shape&amp;quot; around your nose and eyes (but not forehead) which is pretty small, but is #1 lethal thing to aim for. However, rest of the head is a worse target in both &amp;quot;how easy it is to hit&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;how lethal it is&amp;quot; than center of the chest (which is also easiest target to hit), which is #1 target and #2 most lethal area to be hit. <br /> The &amp;quot;stun&amp;quot; thing is actually pretty realistic, because being shot in the head will &amp;quot;stun&amp;quot; you for sure, even if it might not be enough stopping power to get you down. <br /> <br /> In general, game follows reality &amp;quot;aim for the center of the mass, because it's easy and lethal&amp;quot; by making non-aimed shots the most dangerous shots - you get your full dicepool, which translates in more succeses, and with Hurt Locker, you can also get BLEEDING tilt this way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense. The only reason I'm iffy about the stun is that with it only reducing the required damage by 1, you're as likely to stun with a body shot as you are with a head shot, thanks to the -3. I guess that's working as intended, but it really does make armor the only reason you'd ever want to aim for the head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T12:41:05-07:00","id":957116,"title":"","content":"It's really hard to balance aimed shots. I'm glad headshots don't have the potency of blows to the hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T16:22:46-07:00","id":957254,"title":"","content":"because this comes up every so often -<br /> <br /> The way I run it is the narrative is based in the amount of actual damage done. just because you were aiming for the head[or the heart or some other vulnerable area] doesn't mean you connect. If you aim for the head and only score minimal damage, then the blow was glancing. If you score enough damage to kill, then you pretty much blow their head off.<br /> <br /> If you are looking for a short cut to murder, then you can house rule a damage bonus for targeted shots [or as others have suggested, upgrading the damage]. I personally don't recommend that as the system is plenty lethal enough [especially for what is a narrative heavy system].","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T23:54:21-07:00","id":957439,"title":"","content":"Another option: if you aim to the head, gets a &quot;+2 damage&quot;: -3 to attack, but +2 to damage.<br /> It is Hard &amp; Rewarding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T01:13:51-07:00","id":957459,"title":"","content":"Honestly, this kind of misaligned expectation mostly seems to be a result of not understanding that headshot does not mean killshot.<br /> <br /> You take a called shot to the head and get one success (2-3L). Congratulations, you hit them in the head! Your bullet grazes their ear, tearing a chunk of it off.<br /> You got three successes (4-5L)? An angled hit on the cheek, tearing off a fair chunk of face without actually killing them outright.<br /> 5 (6-7L)? A solid hit anywhere on the head. Most people would be bleeding out or be damn close.<br /> <br /> More than that? Traditional killshot, even if they aren't dead /instantly/, they will be without medical attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T01:27:23-07:00","id":957464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956964-reality-vs-game-mechanics?p=957459#post957459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, this kind of misaligned expectation mostly seems to be a result of not understanding that headshot does not mean killshot.<br /> <br /> You take a called shot to the head and get one success (2-3L). Congratulations, you hit them in the head! Your bullet grazes their ear, tearing a chunk of it off.<br /> You got three successes (4-5L)? An angled hit on the cheek, tearing off a fair chunk of face without actually killing them outright.<br /> 5 (6-7L)? A solid hit anywhere on the head. Most people would be bleeding out or be damn close.<br /> <br /> More than that? Traditional killshot, even if they aren't dead /instantly/, they will be without medical attention.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is correct. People can survive even losing encephalic mass - they'll have likely severe sequels, but it's survivable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T02:20:26-07:00","id":957480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956964-reality-vs-game-mechanics?p=957439#post957439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another option: if you aim to the head, gets a &quot;+2 damage&quot;: -3 to attack, but +2 to damage.<br /> It is Hard &amp; Rewarding.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a bad idea.<br /> <br /> You're trading, on average, 1 success for +2 successes. Yes you've lowered your odds of hitting, but since most firearms attacks will ignore defense, you should have very high odds of hitting that can afford the -3.<br /> <br /> This means that as long as you have a decent dice pool, head shots are the default thing to do, which isn't accurate to reality (the default is for center mass) or the game's intent (dramatically interesting combat where the default for maximum damage is normal attacks described to suit the needs of the game and called shots saved for specific situations).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T03:26:37-07:00","id":957495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956964-reality-vs-game-mechanics?p=957480#post957480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This means that as long as you have a decent dice pool, head shots are the default thing to do, which isn't accurate to reality (the default is for center mass)</div> </div> </div> </div>This really can't be understated. <br /> Going for headshots isn't a reality thing, it's a video game thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T03:57:08-07:00","id":957501,"title":"","content":"You are rights Heavy Arms, maybe give a &quot;Size -2&quot; for stun effect, with firearms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T04:03:06-07:00","id":957504,"title":"","content":"It's worth remembering that firearms rules exist in context of cover mechanics, too. Sometimes I feel that people don't use it (and in this case, firearms probably should care about Defense)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T08:28:52-07:00","id":957631,"title":"","content":"Thanks everyone for all the insight. This gives me a lot of rules and things to look into and make sure I understand fully before the next game! Very helpful to hear from people who really understand all of the rules and how they work together. <br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12106-digigirl","name":"Digigirl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T08:38:45-07:00","id":957637,"title":"","content":"This is going to sound weird, but unless you have professional murdergunners who are so invested in murdergunning that they bought combat merits for it, first round of gunfights usually looks like this: everyone spend their action on drawing their weapons, and use up their move action to grab a cover. Round 1, over.<br /> <br /> Gunman with Fast Draw who manages to grab a surprise round can go full Tarantino at his opponents, because they have like 2 rounds of going &quot;pew, pew, pew&quot; before anyone can seriously retailate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}